// expect-trap
// BUG-972: `defer stmt;` is a bare NODE_EXPR_STMT body. It bypassed the per-statement
// wrapper, so it got no IR bounds guard (the emitter's raw-AST guard fired instead and
// re-emitted the defer body inside its own early-return path). It now takes the same
// trapping IR guard as `defer { stmt; }`.
u32[4] arr;
u32 main() {
    u32 i = 0;
    defer arr[i] = 7;
    i = 100;
    return 0;
}
